      "userMessage": "1. Implementation and test results: Revision required. In `src/C_generators.py` (`_build_structure_constants`), your loop for `right_label` is restricted to `ordered_labels[left_index:]`. This means the generator only records the brackets for one ordering. However, `docs/json_schema_specification.md` explicitly requires that each generated file contains \"the complete set of nonzero brackets.\" While your test suite currently reconstructs the $(Y, X)$ brackets using graded symmetry (`basis_bracket`), downstream consumers of the JSON files will expect all nonzero $(X, Y)$ and $(Y, X)$ pairs to be explicitly present.\n2. Please update `_build_structure_constants` to iterate `right_label` over all `ordered_labels` so that both orderings are evaluated and recorded explicitly. After updating the script (and adjusting any test assertions that rely on the old bracket counts), update your proposal in the Response section and stop again for approval. Do not generate the final JSON files yet.",
